From 5af92998d79d88681e7a1bc557820d6fa9e089d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 23:14:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] revdi: expose owned display events to Rust clients

Extend the safe client API with owned DPMS, mode, CRTC, cursor, and DDC/CI events. Cursor and DDC buffers are copied while the C callback is valid, and malloc-owned cursor storage is released at the boundary.

Enable cursor delivery when the owned device opens and provide a safe DDC/CI completion method. No callback pointer or borrowed event payload escapes into a Rust client.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
